The cur_iter increment happens outside the match. According to the issue report,
this causes cur_iter to increment both on Reasoning and Acting passes 
separately, rather than once per complete Reasoning-Acting round.

The goal is to have cur_iter increment once per complete Reasoning-Acting 
iteration.

My plan is to change the code so that cur_iter is incremented only after the 
Acting pass (i.e., after the execution of tool calls), and not after the 
Reasoning pass alone.

I will try to move the increment inside the Acting case, after the tool calls 
execution, while ensuring that if break_execution_for_hitl is True, the 
increment does not occur (to park unfinished round).

I will make a code change for this and then create a small test or script to 
confirm the fix.

