The test still fails because finished_reason is EXCEED_MAX_ITERS instead of 
COMPLETED, meaning the max iteration numbers are exceeded before the final 
answer.

From the debug print:

```
[DEBUG] break_execution_for_hitl=False
```

means break_execution_for_hitl is False so cur_iter should increment to allow 
the last iteration.

The core problem is that the cur_iter is incremented in _next_action just before
returning Reasoning, and also incremented once after the last Acting pass in 
_reply_impl outside match.

This double increment causes cur_iter to increase too fast.

To fix this:

- Remove cur_iter increment from _reply_impl (outside match).

- Keep the increment in _next_action before Reasoning return (counts completed 
cycles).

I will remove the line "self.state.cur_iter += 1" from _reply_impl and rely 
solely on increment in _next_action to count iterations only once per 
reasoning-acting cycle.

